  'A YMCA planned between 1911 and 1913 whose first two floors were finished by the end of 1913; money ran out and the unfinished building stood empty at the west edge of downtown until it opened in November 1927. The register summary calls it a good example of the pre-World War I classical brick YMCA, and one of only a few left in Kansas. Architects were Rose and Peterson. Listed on the National Register in 2019.',
