  "A fifteen-storey hotel finished in August 1951 at 1021 North 7th Street Trafficway, after a decades-long push by city officials and businessmen for a downtown convention hotel. Architect Eugene John Stern began the design in 1929 and altered it when building started. It was the city's largest downtown hotel until 1978, when it was converted to apartments. Listed on the National Register in 2014.",
