  'A three-storey Renaissance Revival building at 1017 North 9th Street, built in 1923 by Rose and Peterson with chemistry and physics laboratories, a home economics department, a two-storey gymnasium and a pool. A tunnel under 9th Street joined it to the high school across the road, which burned in 1934. A junior college then moved in and stayed until 1968. Listed on the National Register in 2012.',
