  'Opened in September 1898 with four teachers when Argentine was booming on the Santa Fe railroad and a silver smelter. The smelter closed and the 1903 flood hit soon after; Argentine joined Kansas City in 1910, and a six-classroom addition followed that year. The school closed in 1973. Romanesque Revival; listed on the National Register in 2013.',
